Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable OTCA path with privacy-first constraints, multi-region residency, dynamic redaction, and compliant purge workflows.

Key Concepts
- Per-tenant residency and data locality
- Dynamic, versioned redaction rules
- Immutable regional logs and global canonical events
- Canary rollouts and zero-downtime config reloads
- GDPR/CCPA purge and auditability

Code Example
```javascript
function redact(event, policy) {
  const out = { ...event };
  if (policy.redactPII && out.user?.email) delete out.user.email;
  if (policy.redactPhone && out.user?.phone) delete out.user.phone;
  return out;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate purge requests across regions with clock skew?
- Which metrics indicate redaction misfires under load and how would you triage them?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design OTCA-compliant governance for feature flags and telemetry with strict residency, immutable records, and secure audit trails.

## Key Concepts

- OTCA residency enforcement
- Write-once ledger (Iceberg/Parquet)
- Region-scoped streaming (Kafka topics)
- Privacy masking for telemetry
- Rollback and rollout testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: region-local validation and masking
function processEvent(event){
  // enforce residency
  if (!inRegion(event.region)) throw new Error("region mismatch");
  // apply masking for sensitive fields
  event.user_id = hash(event.user_id);
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test cross-region policy drift?
- How would you enforce secret binding updates across regions?

